  "description": "This punchy granola gets its warm, bold flavor from instant coffee granules, cinnamon, and vanilla.",
  "notes": "Total time, including resting: 2 hr 45 min.\n\nNotes: I use agave syrup for its mostly neutral flavor. You can substitute with other liquid sweeteners like maple syrup or honey, but they will impart their flavors to the granola. (Maple or honey latte granola, anyone?) Do not substitute with brown sugar or granulated sugar—you’ll end up with powdery and unpleasantly dry granola.\nBe sure to use refined coconut oil, as unrefined oil will give the granola a strong coconut flavor. Any neutral oil (like vegetable or canola) can be substituted for coconut oil.\n\nMake-ahead and storage: Granola can be stored in an airtight container at room temperature for up to 2 weeks.",
